  "unreadable": [],
  "uncertain": [
    "Two USB connectors (USB-A host at top, USB-C at bottom): start end chosen per connector by nearest USB connector, so GPIO/SERVO/DEBUG/Maker ports start at the top/right but the motor terminals start at the bottom.",
    "DEBUG header: SWDIO/GND/SWCLK mapping inferred from the callout order top-to-bottom; the board silkscreen only says DEBUG.",
    "Motor terminals: labelled with the motor output name (M3A etc.); the callout also prints the driving GPIO (GP12...) and PWM channel nearer the pin, kept as functions because the screw terminal is a motor output rather than the GPIO itself."
  ],
  "notes": "Board has two USB connectors (USB-A host at top, USB-C at bottom); each connector starts at its end nearest either USB connector. Skipped: USB host D+/D- callout (USB connector), VIN +/- terminal (polarity marks only), buttons, buzzer, LED. Silkscreen A0-A3 printed beside the GPIO header rows for GP26-GP29 is listed first in functions. SIG/3V3/GND and GND/5V/SIG are column headings."
}
